# Arcturus core (client vs server)

## Hard split

| Layer | Owns | Where |
|-------|------|--------|
| **Server** | Mechanics, stats, loot, AI, scripts | pending SQL + C++ |
| **Client** | Names, icons, Rank text, tooltips, visuals | live Spell Editor DB → Export Spell.dbc → MPQ |

Join keys: `item_template.entry` ↔ Item.dbc; `displayid` ↔ ItemDisplayInfo; spell IDs ↔ Spell.dbc / `spell_dbc`.

## Spell identity (client)

Write names / tooltips / Rank / new IDs into:

`C:\Games\WoW Spell Editor\SpellEditor.db`

via `WoW-Spell-Editor/Arcturus/apply_*.py` (close Spell Editor if DB locked). Apply for the user — do not leave “run this SQL yourself”. Then: reopen editor → Export `Spell.dbc` → MPQ → clear `Cache/WDB`.

Server still owns `spell_dbc` + C++ only. Keep IDs/names aligned.

**Never:** `tools/patch_spell_dbc_*.py`, `spell-patch/`, parallel Spell.dbc folders, or shipping server-only when the player needs client text/icons.

## Spell-kit ship (mechanics on existing abilities)

When scripts attach Brand / redirects / Mandate / pet-bar / stance effects:

1. List every player/pet-facing spell touched (new IDs + **all stock ranks** + parents).
2. Update `SpellDescription0` (cast) and `SpellToolTip0` (aura mouseover — required for visible buffs/debuffs).
3. Mirror Description + AuraDescription in pending `spell_dbc` for custom IDs.
4. Stock ranks stay concise (“Applies Legion Brand”); full numbers live on the dedicated passive/debuff only.

## SQL / build

- World content only in `data/sql/updates/pending_db_*/` (DELETE before INSERT).
- Do not configure/build unless asked. Do not push `live` unless asked.
- Custom learned passives: `PASSIVE` + self-only targets + permanent duration; pet half via `spell_pet_auras`, never `TARGET_UNIT_PET` on the player-learned spell.
- New config keys → `conf/dist/arcturus-recommended-overrides.conf.dist`.

## Research / items

- Stock IDs/icons: Wowhead **`/wotlk/`** only (not Retail).
- Prefer stock `displayid` remaps for icons. Custom entries need `item_dbc` + client Item.dbc / CustomItemFix or they show red `?`.
- After displayid/DBC changes: clear client `Cache/WDB`.

